{"name":"Salsa","hex":"#b31928","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"salsa","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A spicy tomato sauce of Mexican origin, often including onions and hot peppers.","A style of urban music originally from New York heavily influenced by Cuban dance music, jazz and rock."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To dance the salsa."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salsa"}],"entries":[{"title":"Salsa (food)","blocks":[{"text":"A salsa is any of a variety of sauces used as condiments for tacos and other Mexican and Mexican-American foods, and as dips for tortilla chips. They may be raw or cooked, and are generally served at room temperature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Various_salsas.jpg/330px-Various_salsas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salsa_(food)"},{"title":"Salsa music","blocks":[{"text":"Salsa is a style of dance music mainly influenced by Caribbean traditions and music from Cuba, Puerto Rico, the Dominican Republic, and other countries such as Colombia and Venezuela, where African cultural syncretism in music and dance blends with European influences and indigenous instruments, along with contributions from the contiguous United States. Because most of the basic musical components predate the labeling of salsa, there have been many controversies regarding its origin. Most songs considered as salsa are primarily based on son montuno and son cubano, with elements of cha-cha-chá, bolero, rumba, mambo, jazz, R&B, bomba, plena, merengue (Pambiche) and pachanga as well as other music styles from Latin American countries traditions. All of these genres and their musical instruments are adapted and fused to accomplish smooth and seamless transitions between them when performed within the context of salsa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/2006-06-03_Congas1.JPG/330px-2006-06-03_Congas1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salsa_music"},{"title":"Salsa (dance)","blocks":[{"text":"Salsa is the name for Latin American dances that are danced to salsa music. Salsa is one of the most popular types of Latin dance that is practiced worldwide, and is typically danced with a partner, although there are elements of solo footwork as well. There are several distinct styles of salsa that are danced around the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/John_Narvaez_%26_Liz_Rojas_at_California_Dance_Festival_2025_01_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-John_Narvaez_%26_Liz_Rojas_at_California_Dance_Festival_2025_01_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salsa_(dance)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg/500px-MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg/1280px-MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg/500px-MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Salsa made with jalapeños, mango, pineapple, red onion and cilantro (coriander)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMangoPineappleSalsa.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/AGV_4558_%2821982977281%29.jpg/500px-AGV_4558_%2821982977281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/AGV_4558_%2821982977281%29.jpg/1280px-AGV_4558_%2821982977281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u